== 1. the scan finds every action and names every group ==
ok   the actions this executable answers: broken.detached, broken.generic, broken.hidden, broken.wrapped_dto, broken.wrong_argument, broken.wrong_error, broken.wrong_reply, notes.count, notes.describe, notes.publish, notes.save, twice.clash
ok   notes.save is usable: found
ok     its parameters: id, body
ok     its reply: Result<string, string>
ok     read as a Result: true
ok   notes.publish carries its roles: 1
ok   a refused action is not routable: gone

== 2. a call, its arguments and its reply ==
ok   a Result that succeeded: {"ok":true,"k":"ok","v":"note 7: hello","e":""}
ok   a Result that failed: {"ok":false,"k":"failed","v":null,"e":"a note needs a body"}
ok   a DTO in and a DTO out: {"ok":true,"k":"ok","v":{"stamp":"a note","size":12,"clean":true},"e":""}
ok   three scalars, one of them a float: {"ok":true,"k":"ok","v":12,"e":""}
ok   and a whole number is a float too: {"ok":true,"k":"ok","v":8,"e":""}

== 3. what a call is refused for, before it runs ==
ok   an action nobody declared: no action is named "notes.nowhere"
ok   an argument that is missing: notes.save: the argument "body" is missing
ok   an argument of the wrong type: notes.save: "id" is not an int
ok   a body that is not JSON: invalid
ok   a body that is not an object: notes.save: the arguments must be a JSON object
ok   a DTO argument that is not an object: notes.describe: "draft" is a latte$entry.Draft and must be a JSON object
ok   a role the caller does not have: forbidden
ok   and the same call from somebody who does: {"ok":true,"k":"ok","v":"published 1","e":""}

== 4. every fault site in actions.b ==
-- a-dto-field-that-cannot-cross
   site:    dto_plan_for / a field that cannot cross
   fault:   latte$entry.Bad.tags is a List<string>, which cannot cross a server action; a field of a DTO is a string, an int, a bool or a float
   control: (quiet)
ok   a-dto-field-that-cannot-cross: the exact fault: latte$entry.Bad.tags is a List<string>, which cannot cross a server action; a field of a DTO is a string, an int, a bool or a float
ok   a-dto-field-that-cannot-cross: the control is quiet: (quiet)
-- an-action-outside-a-group
   site:    scan_actions / @action on a type that is not @actions
   fault:   latte$entry.Stray.wander is annotated @action but latte$entry.Stray is not annotated @actions, so nothing would ever route to it
   control: (quiet)
ok   an-action-outside-a-group: the exact fault: latte$entry.Stray.wander is annotated @action but latte$entry.Stray is not annotated @actions, so nothing would ever route to it
ok   an-action-outside-a-group: the control is quiet: (quiet)
-- a-group-name-a-url-cannot-carry
