-- a-result-of-a-class
   site:    plan_for_action / a Result of something that is not a scalar
   fault:   latte$entry.BrokenActions.wrapped_dto answers Result<latte$entry.Saved, string>; latte can read a Result of a string, an int, a bool or a float, and not of a class — reading one back needs the closed type spelled out and a dispatcher only has a descriptor. Answer the latte$entry.Saved directly and carry the failure in a field of it, or answer a Result of one scalar
   control: (quiet)
ok   a-result-of-a-class: the exact fault: latte$entry.BrokenActions.wrapped_dto answers Result<latte$entry.Saved, string>; latte can read a Result of a string, an int, a bool or a float, and not of a class — reading one back needs the closed type spelled out and a dispatcher only has a descriptor. Answer the latte$entry.Saved directly and carry the failure in a field of it, or answer a Result of one scalar
